<p><strong>Looking for a greenlight:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Slightly Emotional, Slightly Drama</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Anomalous humanoid entities. Every SCP has the ability to &quot;project&quot; emotions onto others, the effect is amplified on other SCP-XXXX instances.</li>
<li>Although not stated in the article itself. It is hinted at that after a prolonged conversation (Relating to the SCPs emotion) the anomaly will 'imprint' on the other participant. Imprinting means that the SCP-XXXX instance will follow and project emotions onto the person who was imprinted on.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> After an experiment. A researcher accidentally gets an entity to follow him around, The resulting projection throws off his work and messes up the article. The article will be presented in an empathetic and happy tone. The Special Containment Procedures will be a battle of the empathy of the SCP and the coldness of the Foundation (line by line). The Description will be an optimistic look at the anomaly, Showing each one to be nicer than it actually is. The Addendums will start with a look at the situation by our main researcher, followed by other's opinions.</p>
<p><strong>Aditional Notes:</strong> None as of now</p>

