			<div class="content" id="post-content-4820230">
									

<p>Thanks for looking over my concept. I meant to edit it overnight but ran out of time. I have some things I want to clarify.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Clarification</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>At the end of the day, my feeling on this is it needs more narrative oomph.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I agree with this. The idea wasn't formed from a story, So when I decided to try and get the concept greenlighted, I felt I needed a narrative to keep it interesting. I was thinking about how merging would place more power on the entity. To keep it stable, it would expel some sort of energy. The more that merge, the more energy expelled. Also, I understand how cliche containment breaches are, and that might have been what made my concept feel so eh.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>'greedy' implies they can use this SCP for some kinda…benefit? But like, it's really not clear how they could 'get greedy' here or indeed why the merging could cause an explosion.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I couldn't think of a word other than greedy. My implication was that the foundation believed merging to be safer than it actually was. I like your ideas on how to use the word 'greedy' in my concept. Although I don't think that would make some sort of accident happen.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(Immortal, but that doesn't really matter)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not too sure why I wrote this. I was meaning that the immortality aspect of the SCP wasn't the main focus. It was more of a fate keeping the entities alive. I now see that my idea was to make an SCP that was bound to fate, like everything that happened to them happened for a reason. The reason they are drawn together is because of that fate.</p>
<p>I might scrap the idea of a dimensional rift and replace it with the idea of fate. Again I would like ideas on how to do that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>I will edit my concept and wait for a response.</p>
<p>I will also reformat the concept to the guidelines to make it more readable.</p>

