			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825860">
									

<p>This all feels fairly vague. You get 400 words in the last four sections of the post to expand upon your idea, so I think that you should attempt to explore this further.</p>
<p>What are the stakes of this anomaly?</p>
<p>Also why couldn't the foundation just lock these people up and forget about them? (<em>this is in response to your post saying that the anomalous human follows the researcher around</em>)</p>
<p>Happy tone aside, what will you do to get the reader to feel invested in these events? Is there someone we can relate to?</p>
<p>What is the narrative journey of the article? Where do we start and then where do we end?</p>
<p>Other than the happy tone, what is the thematic core to your article?</p>
<p><em><strong>I would suggest answering these questions for yourself and then editing the original post. Then let me know if you want further comments.</strong></em></p>

